{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790735015,"nonce":"3tc6Cl6EVuvd1XneMyuv3dlt+nU=","title":"Reflect mixed enum constructors with their compiled representation","message":"Type.allEnums returned raw discriminants for parameterless constructors even when the enum had payload constructors. Rayzor compiles all values of such an enum as boxed [tag, fields] values. Reflection then produced null constructor names and Array.join rendered null or pointer values. Type.createEnum and Type.createEnumIndex had the same representation split for parameterless constructors.\n\nThe runtime now constructs reflected values using the registered enum layout, records their type so Type.enumConstructor can recover it after generic erasure, and keeps the type on arrays returned by Type.allEnums for generic joins. Array\u003cEnum\u003e.join also uses its known enum type when available. EnumReflectionValues covers mixed and plain enums, joins, constructor names, indexes and reflective construction.\n\nBefore: 782/1094 scored passes in /tmp/rayzor-bytesdata-final2-full/report.tsv. After: 783/1094 in /tmp/rayzor-enum-full/report.tsv. Issue3389 changes WRONG_ANSWER to PASS with no other status changes. TestType advances past its allEnums assertion to an unrelated array type-unification failure. All 95 authored regressions pass.\n\nThe required cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings run stops on existing warnings in runtime/src/profile.rs and runtime/src/type_system.rs. Clippy for compiler and rayzor-runtime passes with those known warnings and one existing compiler warning excluded. Formatting passes.","files":null}]}